## Focus mix: 40 Hz gamma + 24 Hz beta binaural beats over a BROWN-noise bed
##
## Same beat structure as focus-40-24-pink.sbg (180/40 Hz gamma pair,
## 320/24 Hz high-beta pair).  Brown noise is not built into sbagen, so
## it is mixed in from a soundtrack file: an OGG used with -m loops
## forever by default (full-length segments, 1s crossfade), so a short
## file covers any session length.
##
## Regenerate the bed to taste (mono->stereo, ~2 min is plenty):
##   ffmpeg -y -f lavfi -i anoisesrc=color=brown:r=44100:a=0.6 \
##     -ac 2 -t 120 -c:a libvorbis -q:a 4 sequences/brown-noise.ogg
##
## Run from the repo root so the -m path resolves.
##
## Headphones required -- binaural beats collapse on speakers.
##
## Play live (ALSA build, stops after the hour):
##   dev/sbagen-fixed sequences/focus-40-24-brown.sbg
## Render 30 minutes to a file:
##   LENGTH=00:30:00 ./mksounds.sh focus-40-24-brown sequences/focus-40-24-brown.sbg

-m sequences/brown-noise.ogg

all-off: -

focus-40-24-brown: mix/30 180+40/30 320+24/25

0:00:00 focus-40-24-brown
1:00:00 all-off
